  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $1\\leq a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ be a sequence of integers such that no $a_i$ is the sum of consecutive $a_j$ for $j<i$. Is it true that $ \\limsup \\frac{a_n}{n}=\\infty? $ Or even $ \\lim \\frac{1}{\\log x}\\sum_{a_n<x}\\frac{1}{a_n}=0? $ ",
